    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f046b7ecdaf3c5ffda74d03b9688d4737df50554ec33bf16cffe0c277bbd5ed2",
      "text": "After breakfast, take a tour of Arequipa.\n\nSpanish conquistadors founded the city in the 16th century. It lies in a fertile valley at more than **2,300 metres** above sea level, surrounded by three volcanoes: **Misti, Chachani and Pichu Pichu**.\n\nMost of its historic buildings were built with pale stone, earning Arequipa the name White City.\n\nThe historic centre has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since **2000**.\n\nOn the tour, visit the main square, the **Yanahuara** viewpoint and **Santa Catalina Monastery**, founded in the late 16th century.\n\nThe monastery covers about **20 square kilometres**. The complex has more than **100 rooms**, including a church, galleries, gardens and a picture gallery with works of religious art.\n\nAt the scheduled time, transfer to the airport and fly to Lima.\n\nOn arrival, you will be met and transferred to your hotel for check-in.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-20261110-5190562f69e7b764",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      }
    },
